Floor remained 1, XP increased 45 (floor clear reward 45) and shards +34. So descend was triggered and rewarded, but loadFloor after 520ms maybe did not complete by 2s? Wait mode playing, floor 1. Maybe the setTimeout in descend ran but `game.mode !== 'playing'`? Let's trace descend:
```
game.fade=1;
game.mode='transition';
setTimeout(() => { if (game.mode === 'transition') game.mode='playing'; },520);
setTimeout(() => { if (game.mode !== 'playing') return; loadFloor(floor+1,false); ...},520);
```
Order of setTimeout: the loadFloor timeout registered first, then mode timeout. At 520, loadFloor callback checks game.mode !== 'playing' — mode is still 'transition' (because the other timeout runs after) → return! Then mode set playing. So floor never loads. This is an ordering bug in existing code. Need fix descend: don't gate on playing before transition ends. Either set mode playing immediately before loadFloor or reorder. Simplest:

```
setTimeout(() => {
  game.mode='playing';
  loadFloor(floor+1,false);
  ...
}, 520);
game.fade=1;
game.mode='transition';
```
Remove second timeout. Also carefully if user pauses? no.

Fix.

